    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian Bulk and Allied (IBA) consignment bilty is a transport document that records the consignor, consignee, vehicle details, and the agreed freight terms. It must be signed by both parties and stamped by the IBA authority.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>In addition to these core documents, it is highly advisable to secure a <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>. This type of coverage protects the vehicle against loss, damage, or theft during the entire marine transit phase, regardless of the cause.</p>
<p>The insurance is calculated as a percentage of the vehicle’s declared value, typically 100%, ensuring that the full replacement cost is covered. This coverage is especially critical when the vehicle is being moved across coastal routes or over water bodies, where risks are higher and recovery costs can be substantial.</p>
<p>To obtain the 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance, the consignor should provide the following to the insurer:</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Vehicle details: make, model, year, VIN, and current market value.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Route information: origin, destination, and any intermediate stops.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Transport method: details of the carrier, vessel, and handling procedures.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Proof of ownership: original RC and a notarized statement of ownership.</span></li>
</ul>
<p>Once the insurance policy is in place, the insurer will issue a certificate that must be affixed to the consignment bilty. This certificate should be retained in the vehicle’s transport file and presented to the carrier and any regulatory authorities upon request.</p>
<p>By ensuring that all these documents are complete, accurate, and up‑to‑date, the vehicle owner can mitigate legal risks, streamline the transport process, and guarantee that the vehicle arrives safely at its destination in Bethamcherla.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



